cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI-StatPaper-PhD: a gated pipeline, prompt library and skill pack for writing PhD-level statistics papers with AI"
message: >-
  If you use this project, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: chenyiadam
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenyiadam/AI-StatPaper-PhD.git"
url: "https://github.com/chenyiadam/AI-StatPaper-PhD"
abstract: >-
  An open-source engineering project for statistics PhD students and
  early-career researchers that turns "writing papers with AI" into an
  executable, auditable, reproducible pipeline: a seven-stage gated
  workflow (research question, literature, theory, experiments, writing,
  mock review, journal adaptation & submission), 32 copy-paste prompts,
  9 installable agent skills, 7 checklists, 4 deterministic check scripts
  (citation consistency, notation, figures/tables, AI-flavor symbols),
  reproducible templates (JASA-style LaTeX, Quarto, R/Python simulation
  skeletons), and 9 statistics-journal style profiles for reshaping a
  draft into venue-ready form.
keywords:
  - statistics
  - academic writing
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
  - peer review
  - scholarly writing
